    "case_id": "exploration-local-stress",
    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 12 USER]\ne277\tThank you.\ne278\tI'm going to sit with this for a minute.\ne279\tI'll let you know how it goes.\n[Turn 12 ASSISTANT]\ne280\tYou're welcome.\ne281\tOne more thing before you go.\ne282\tYou are going to second-guess every single one of these steps this week.\ne283\tYou're going to wake up at 3am convinced you should have called the police.\ne284\tYou're going to read her one-word text and convince yourself it means she hates you.\ne285\tYou're going to be tempted to take her phone, block the guy, and lock things down because it feels like doing something.\ne286\tWhen that happens, remember: the goal isn't to feel like you did enough.\ne287\tThe goal is for her to come out the other side of this as a kid who can tell you things.\ne288\tThose are not the same goal, and the first one — the \"doing enough\" feeling — will actively work against the second one.\ne289\tYou're not overreacting.\ne290\tYour ex is wrong.\ne291\tAnd you also don't have to react as hard as your fear wants you to.\ne292\tBoth things are true.",
      "citation_allowed": true,
